# v11 flight-board connectivity registry -- SOURCE OF TRUTH for pin->net.
#
# DERIVED FROM connectivity/v10_pinmap.reg AT master 04219c23 BY ADDING THE ADR-148
# ANALOG-SENSE BLOCK.  Every v10 row is carried through unchanged.  The one inherited
# net whose CONNECTIVITY changes is the /VSCAP divider midpoint, and it is called out
# here rather than buried:
#
#   v10:  R_DIV1.2 /SCAP_ADC   R_DIV2.1 /SCAP_ADC        (net ended at a dead pad)
#   v11:  R_DIV1.2 /SCAP_DIV   R_DIV2.1 /SCAP_DIV        (divider midpoint)
#         /SCAP_DIV -- R_PROT1 --> /SCAP_ADC --> U_ADC2.4  (now TERMINATES on an ADC pin)
#
# The terminating net keeps the old name on purpose: /SCAP_ADC is what the ADRs and the
# firmware already refer to.
#
# THERE IS NO v11 BOARD.  No hub_board_v11.kicad_pcb exists; nothing here is derived from
# copper and registry.py gen/check cannot run against v11 until one does.  This file drives
# tracker/hardware/build_v11_sch.py, the schematic generator.
#
# v11 SCOPE -- all four operator-approved items, none silently dropped:
#   item 1  D_BP1..D_BP4 moved to the TOP face (ADR-146)  -- LAYOUT-ONLY, ZERO parts.
#           NOT DONE.  PR #530 measured that the two proposed D_BP2 top sites are illegal
#           under native DRC; accepted, not re-litigated.  No registry row can express a
#           face change, so this file is untouched by item 1.
#   item 2  /SCAP_ADC + solar-input dividers (ADR-148)    -- THIS FILE.
#   item 3  real cut-driver parts (latch/AO3400A/...)     -- NOT DONE.  U_CUT1..4 remain
#           placeholder footprints.  Their FOUR ADS1115 channels are RESERVED here.
#   item 4  GPIO economy / MCP23017 (ADR-145)             -- NOT DONE.  No part added.
#
# Format: REF.PIN  NET  # authority
# UNASSIGNED = the pin has no net. Those are listed at the end of this file.

# --- U1  (ESP32-S3-WROOM-1U)
U1.1  GND  # v9 netlist (rails)
U1.2  +3V3  # v9 netlist (rails)
U1.3  /EN  # ADR-121 (J_PROG)
